{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following is NOT an antiderivative of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06dc918f8b7700e8637454c2d98382de60651e06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x \\cos x$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d1123208bca1badc4ecde775995c25a00f5a93a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\cos(2x)  \\quad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{4} \\left( \\sin^{2}x - \\cos^{2}x \\right)  \\quad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{2} \\sin^{2}x  \\quad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\cos(2x)  \\quad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ -\\dfrac{1}{2}\\cos^{2}x  \\quad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"737\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06dc918f8b7700e8637454c2d98382de60651e06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x \\cos x$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84b225cc3eaf412fef61276995290fcbd486b8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\sin{(2x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"38\" />. The integral of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fa1992f3757578c2b3de1725b505066ca482562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{(2x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/52841b66bc0f46a6bc10e74c96ae37dea701b670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\cos{(2x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"38\" />, so half of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/05182f27658f076cdf5e5f58b8c8d39f1c29d9d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-1}{4}\\cos{(2x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b7e8e80615b1d29eef55381fc9b2bad52cb52bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\cos(2x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"145\" height=\"49\" /> is two times this, so it cannot be antiderivative of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06dc918f8b7700e8637454c2d98382de60651e06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x \\cos x$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2025 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=